    "created_at": "2016-04-08T21:56:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-08T21:56:50Z",
    "body": "There's no guarantee that an `<input type=date>` displays in the \"standard Western calendar\" fashion. At some point in the past, Android's UI was just a month/day/year set of spinners.  (It's currently a monthly calendar, tho.)  In countries that traditionally use a different calendar than the Gregorian, it might display in that calendar.  The only requirement is that the `.value` of the input be a Gregorian data in a specific format that the spec describes.\n\nSo, there's no guarantee that the \"first day of the week\" will even be meaningful.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
